            <ArticleTitle>Right heart assist during beating bypass for severe left ventricular dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7; discussion 158-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three patients with triple-vessel disease and severe left ventricular dysfunction underwent successful revascularization on a beating heart, using a right ventricular assist system. Heparin-coated circuits with a centrifugal pump provided 2.5 to 3.5 L x min(-1) of flow to maintain good hemodynamics and enable easy access to the posterior vessels during vertical displacement of the heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
